# kube-state-metrics custom resource state configuration (issue 149), rendered by Terraform (infra/monitoring.tf) and mounted only
# when monitoring_nodeclaim_metrics_enabled is true. Nothing here is a secret.
#
# It exposes two series for the NodeClaim objects of node auto-provisioning (Karpenter, which runs in the AKS-managed control plane;
# only its custom resources are readable from the cluster):
#
#   kube_customresource_nodeclaim_created_timestamp_seconds                      metadata.creationTimestamp, Unix seconds
#   kube_customresource_nodeclaim_condition_last_transition_timestamp_seconds    lastTransitionTime of each status condition, Unix seconds
#
# Time to node, step by step, is the second series minus the first for the conditions Launched, Registered and Initialized
# (infra/monitoring/alert-rules.json, the recording rule factory:nodeclaim_condition_seconds).
#
# UNVERIFIED, none of it was started against a cluster:
#   * the version below: the NodePool object of this repository (worker_pool.tf) uses karpenter.sh/v1, so v1 is the expectation, but
#     which version NAP serves for NodeClaim is not recorded (kubectl get crd nodeclaims.karpenter.sh -o jsonpath='{.spec.versions[*].name}');
#   * that kube-state-metrics turns an RFC 3339 string at `valueFrom` into Unix seconds (its documentation describes numbers and
#     timestamps; the pinned version was not run). If it does not, the second series is empty or the pod logs an error, and the pod
#     series (kube_pod_created, kube_pod_status_ready_time) still give time to node;
#   * the exact name that results from the default metric name prefix `kube_customresource_` plus `name:` below;
#   * how this version behaves when the CRD does not exist (a cluster without NAP): that is why this file is mounted only on request.
#
# `name` is a per-object label (Karpenter generates it, `<nodepool>-<random>`; no issue or repository text). The series need it to be
# unique, and every query and recording rule aggregates it away (a NodeClaim lives as long as its node).
kind: CustomResourceStateMetrics
spec:
  resources:
    - groupVersionKind:
        group: karpenter.sh
        kind: NodeClaim
        version: ${api_version}
      labelsFromPath:
        name: [metadata, name]
        nodepool: [metadata, labels, karpenter.sh/nodepool]
      metrics:
        - name: nodeclaim_created_timestamp_seconds
          help: Creation time of the NodeClaim, Unix seconds.
          each:
            type: Gauge
            gauge:
              path: [metadata, creationTimestamp]
        - name: nodeclaim_condition_last_transition_timestamp_seconds
          help: Last transition time of each status condition of the NodeClaim, Unix seconds.
          each:
            type: Gauge
            gauge:
              path: [status, conditions]
              labelsFromPath:
                type: [type]
                status: [status]
              valueFrom: [lastTransitionTime]
